  "term": "snare",
  "says": "Reid's snare drum: two things at once - a drum body (a tuned tone around 150-250 Hz with a fast pitch drop and a short decay) and the snares (a burst of noise, band-passed in the mids, decaying a little slower than the body). Signature: an instant attack, a decay to -20 dB in 50-400 ms, a spectrum flat enough to be heard as noise but with the body's bump, dead silent after.",
